                "reply_count": 51,
                "retweet_count": 28,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "What is happening in Springfield is tragic.\u00a0\n\nSpringfield has a population of about 60,000 people, but the 15,000 to 20,000 Haitian migrants that were flown into the community have put a significant strain on housing, hospitals, and schools.\n\nI hosted Mayor Rob Rue in Washington, D.C., to meet senior officials from the U.S. Department of Homeland Security and the U.S. Department of Labor to detail the impacts of the Biden-Harris Administration\u2019s policies and request assistance for our community, but they declined to help.\n\nPresident Biden and Vice President Harris have refused to step up to the plate and recognize the consequences of their actions, not only to the City of Springfield but also to the Haitian population.",
